# Hourly bounded read of the paths launchd jobs depend on (local-volume-probe,
# sd:2541). On 2026-10-01 every launchd job that opened a file on the external
# volume waited for 16 hours while interactive sessions kept writing to it;
# nothing said so until the jobs' own timeouts ran out (sd:2537). This job
# runs `status` in launchd context, the context that stalled, and exits 1
# naming each path still waiting at VOLUME_PROBE_TIMEOUT, so the failure
# notification fires within the hour. The nightly health check runs the same
# `status` through its sweep; this job only shortens the wait.
JOB_SCHEDULE="5 * * * *"
JOB_COMMAND="sh \"$ROOT/../local-volume-probe/volume-probe.sh\" status"
